WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:05.055
Olga asks the robot agent to put the red dishes in the bin.

00:05.055 --> 00:06.269
It refuses.

00:06.269 --> 00:08.193
Not because the AI is unsure,

00:08.193 --> 00:11.245
but because that skill never earned a licence.

00:11.245 --> 00:14.787
On our Nebius GPU, NVIDIA's GR00T managed

00:14.787 --> 00:17.724
only 14 of 40 tries in simulation.

00:18.520 --> 00:20.158
This is Learner's Permit:

00:20.158 --> 00:24.023
an AI may command a robot skill only after trials prove it,

00:24.023 --> 00:28.085
only where it was tested, and only until the evidence changes.

00:28.085 --> 00:30.818
Nemotron plans on Nebius Token Factory,

00:30.818 --> 00:34.251
but its only path to the robot is one checkpoint.

00:34.251 --> 00:36.697
There, a Cedar policy, the licence,

00:36.697 --> 00:39.563
and live web checks decide every request.

00:40.360 --> 00:42.773
Licences are earned in simulation.

00:42.773 --> 00:47.509
Bananas into the bin: 37 successes in 40 GR00T episodes.

00:47.509 --> 00:51.352
The gate is plain statistics: we're 97.6 percent sure

00:51.352 --> 00:54.614
the true success rate is at least 80 percent,

00:54.614 --> 00:56.427
above the 95 percent bar.

00:56.427 --> 01:00.189
So the AI may now command it, at the speed that was tested.

01:00.189 --> 01:04.645
The same sweep also runs as a Nebius Serverless AI Job:

01:04.645 --> 01:08.615
71 of 80, licensed, for about a cent per episode.

01:09.430 --> 01:12.757
The web can only narrow a licence, never widen it.

01:12.757 --> 01:15.978
This skill is licensed for parts up to one kilogram.

01:15.978 --> 01:18.756
Asked to move a cordless drill kit,

01:18.756 --> 01:22.168
Tavily finds its spec sheet: 1.7 kilograms.

01:22.168 --> 01:24.199
Denied, with the source cited.

01:24.199 --> 01:28.310
Then a grease gun: Tavily finds an official recall notice.

01:28.310 --> 01:31.531
Denied again, and Nemotron explains what to do next.

01:32.330 --> 01:33.698
Then we changed the scene.

01:33.698 --> 01:35.098
GR00T still succeeded,

01:35.098 --> 01:38.217
but the licence was evidence about the old scene.

01:38.217 --> 01:41.146
After each run, Nemotron's vision model compares

01:41.146 --> 01:44.563
the camera frame with the one the licence was earned on.

01:44.563 --> 01:46.892
It saw the floor change from tile to wood,

01:46.892 --> 01:49.055
so the licence was revoked on the spot,

01:49.055 --> 01:51.162
before the robot had a chance to fail.

01:51.162 --> 01:54.570
Olga's next request was denied, with an explanation,

01:54.570 --> 01:57.388
and the agent goes back to asking a person.

01:58.180 --> 02:01.315
One application of Learner's Permit is crop health.

02:01.315 --> 02:05.044
In 2024, disease cut US corn yields six percent

02:05.044 --> 02:10.281
and soybeans over five: nearly seven billion dollars, by our math.

02:10.281 --> 02:12.577
The licence works for any model.

02:12.577 --> 02:16.332
Few-shot leaf diagnosis with Nemotron's vision model

02:16.332 --> 02:18.426
earned a licence for peppers,

02:18.426 --> 02:21.675
but not for tomatoes: 85 of 100 isn't enough.

02:21.675 --> 02:25.453
A ResNet we fine-tuned on a Nebius GPU in under a minute

02:25.453 --> 02:29.500
earned both, and each licence is pinned to that exact model.

02:30.300 --> 02:33.227
This is the system our team designed for the field:

02:33.227 --> 02:35.637
drones and ground robots feed crop models,

02:35.637 --> 02:37.990
and every action goes through the permit.

02:37.990 --> 02:40.021
What's lit already runs on Nebius.

02:40.021 --> 02:43.807
The drones, thermal cameras and navigation come next.

02:44.610 --> 02:47.144
Other robot agents ask when they're unsure.

02:47.144 --> 02:48.922
Ours asks when it's unproven.

02:48.922 --> 02:51.427
Learner's Permit: cultivating trust,

02:51.427 --> 02:53.237
one robot skill at a time.
